<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!--
  Associates (D107). The 54 Associate records describe their creature only
  as a prose stat block; the content import parses it into a typed field and
  4ecb prints one associate card per creature the character has, with the
  master-relative numbers worked out (rules-engine associates.ts).

  1. Which associates a character has is the native signal the content
     already uses: a FREEBEE:<associate id> stat (Elemental Companion, Summon
     Warlock's Ally (Elemental), Demonic Companion, Summon Sidhe Ally, …).
     Four sources lack it and give the creature only through a community
     card (CBLoader/Custom/36-companion.part and Tivaan's companion cards):
     the Fey Beast Tamer companion choice, Summon Natural Ally (whose cards
     carry the Primal Guardian/Predator and 15th/29th-level gates), Unleash
     Monolith and Summon Flame Zephyr. Those cards now carry the FREEBEE
     instead (a structure fix, D089).
  2. Every community card that restates an associate's stat block becomes an
     inert Internal record under the same ID, so imported characters still
     resolve and no duplicate power card prints (as 91-familiar-cards.part
     and 99-companions.part do). The Fey Beast Tamer and Demon Companion
     choices keep granting their per-level helpers (Tivaan's "Fey Beast
     Companion: Blink Dog N", "Demon Companion: Quasit N"): legacy saves
     store all 29 of them, so removing the grants would orphan the saved
     occurrences. They only rewrite the inert card's fields, so they have no
     effect.
  3. Two stat blocks lost text in the content, restored from the D&D Insider
     compendium entries (iws.mx associate64 and associate57):
     - Living Zephyr (Heroes of the Elemental Chaos p. 62): the 13th- and
       23rd-level steps of Animal Attack dropped their dice and flat bonus.
     - Sidhe House Guard (Heroes of the Feywild p. 109): "highest ability
       modifier", not "Primary ability".
-->
<D20Rules game-system="D&amp;D4E">
  <!-- 1 and 2. The community cards. -->

  <!-- Fey Beast Tamer (Heroes of the Feywild): the companion choice gives the creature only through the card. -->
  <RulesElement name="Trained Blink Dog" type="Internal" source="4ecb corrections" internal-id="ID_TIV_FEY_BEAST_COMPANION-1-2"><rules><statadd name="FREEBEE:ID_FMP_ASSOCIATE_53" value="+1" /></rules></RulesElement>
  <RulesElement name="Trained Displacer Beast" type="Internal" source="4ecb corrections" internal-id="ID_TIV_FEY_BEAST_COMPANION-1"><rules><statadd name="FREEBEE:ID_FMP_ASSOCIATE_54" value="+1" /></rules></RulesElement>
  <RulesElement name="Trained Fey Panther" type="Internal" source="4ecb corrections" internal-id="ID_TIV_FEY_BEAST_COMPANION-1-3"><rules><statadd name="FREEBEE:ID_FMP_ASSOCIATE_55" value="+1" /></rules></RulesElement>
  <RulesElement name="Trained Young Owlbear" type="Internal" source="4ecb corrections" internal-id="ID_TIV_FEY_BEAST_COMPANION-1-4"><rules><statadd name="FREEBEE:ID_FMP_ASSOCIATE_56" value="+1" /></rules></RulesElement>

  <!-- Summon Natural Ally (Heroes of the Feywild): the cards carry the aspect and level gates of the summons. -->
  <RulesElement name="Primal Guardian Ally: Giant Cobra" type="Internal" source="4ecb corrections" internal-id="ID_TIV_NATURAL_ALLY-1"><rules><statadd name="FREEBEE:ID_FMP_ASSOCIATE_40" value="+1" /></rules></RulesElement>
  <RulesElement name="Primal Guardian Ally: Desert Hawk" type="Internal" source="4ecb corrections" internal-id="ID_TIV_NATURAL_ALLY-2"><rules><statadd name="FREEBEE:ID_FMP_ASSOCIATE_42" value="+1" /></rules></RulesElement>
